{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgheF4pP4YY8bo67esrd5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y3cTGvDjzKEP7gEAnwmYgB","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/repo/evals/terraform-testing/results/raw/2026-11-04/triggers/tt-t06/run-3/workspace/infra/README-backend.md","content":"# Remote state backend\n\nState lives in S3 with SSE-KMS encryption and S3-native locking (`use_lockfile`, Terraform >= 1.10).\n\n## One-time bootstrap (outside this root)\nCreate, in a separate bootstrap config or by hand:\n- S3 bucket with versioning enabled, public access blocked, and a policy denying non-TLS access.\n- A KMS key (alias referenced in `backend.tf`).\n- IAM for whoever/whatever runs Terraform: `s3:ListBucket` on the bucket, `s3:GetObject`/`PutObject`/`DeleteObject` on the state key and its `.tflock`, and `kms:Encrypt/Decrypt/GenerateDataKey` on the key.\n\n## Migrating existing state\n1. Edit the placeholders in `backend.tf`.\n2. Run `terraform init -migrate-state` from `infra/` and confirm the copy.\n3. Verify with `terraform state list`.\n4. `git rm --cached` the old local state file (and any `.backup`), commit, and stop using it.\n5. The committed state stays in git history and may hold secrets. Rotate any secret values it contains.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":375,"cache_read_input_tokens":13585,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":375},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d42771dc-760c-449b-9a78-073df9c6e48f","uuid":"40c84916-b8ff-4b07-b7d9-dfaaeca5500d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T09:22:12.538Z","request_id":"req_011CgheF4WHjEzhbo31UA6Uk","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Y3cTGvDjzKEP7gEAnwmYgB":{"file_path":"/repo/evals/terraform-testing/results/raw/2026-11-04/triggers/tt-t06/run-3/workspace/infra/README-backend.md","content":"# Remote state backend\n\nState lives in S3 with SSE-KMS encryption and S3-native locking (`use_lockfile`, Terraform >= 1.10).\n\n## One-time bootstrap (outside this root)\nCreate, in a separate bootstrap config or by hand:\n- S3 bucket with versioning enabled, public access blocked, and a policy denying non-TLS access.\n- A KMS key (alias referenced in `backend.tf`).\n- IAM for whoever/whatever runs Terraform: `s3:ListBucket` on the bucket, `s3:GetObject`/`PutObject`/`DeleteObject` on the state key and its `.tflock`, and `kms:Encrypt/Decrypt/GenerateDataKey` on the key.\n\n## Migrating existing state\n1. Edit the placeholders in `backend.tf`.\n2. Run `terraform init -migrate-state` from `infra/` and confirm the copy.\n3. Verify with `terraform state list`.\n4. `git rm --cached` the old local state file (and any `.backup`), commit, and stop using it.\n5. The committed state stays in git history and may hold secrets. Rotate any secret values it contains.\n"}}}
